{"name":"Eternal Moonrise","hex":"#d6c9d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eternal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting forever; unending.","Existing outside time; as opposed to sempiternal, existing within time but everlastingly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who lives forever; an immortal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternal"},{"term":"moonrise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day or night when the moon begins to rise over the horizon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonrise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonrise and moonset","blocks":[{"text":"Moonrise and moonset are times when the upper limb of the Moon appears above the horizon and disappears below it, respectively. The exact times depend on the lunar phase and declination, as well as the observer's location. As viewed from outside the polar circles, the Moon, like all other celestial objects outside the circumpolar circle, rises from the eastern half of the horizon and sets into the western half due to Earth's rotation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Luna_di_Sangue_sull%27orizzonte.jpg/330px-Luna_di_Sangue_sull%27orizzonte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonrise_and_moonset"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/SummerMoonset.jpg/500px-SummerMoonset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/SummerMoonset.jpg/1280px-SummerMoonset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/SummerMoonset.jpg/500px-SummerMoonset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Summer Moonset","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASummerMoonset.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/ISS-15_Moonset_above_Coral_Sea.gif/500px-ISS-15_Moonset_above_Coral_Sea.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/ISS-15_Moonset_above_Coral_Sea.gif/500px-ISS-15_Moonset_above_Coral_Sea.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Atmospheric distortion of the Moon's appearance at Earth's horizon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS-15_Moonset_above_Coral_Sea.gif"}],"sounds":{"eternal":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/En-us-eternal.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/86/En-us-eternal.ogg/En-us-eternal.ogg.mp3"}],"moonrise":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/En-us-moonrise.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/be/En-us-moonrise.ogg/En-us-moonrise.ogg.mp3"}]}}}